Result
------
The Release x64 build completed successfully. Production endpoint diagnostics,
native Socket.IO signaling, LiveKit connection, and the camera pixel roundtrip
also completed successfully. The job failed when launching:

  native-windows/build/Release/LuniraAgoraRoundtrip.exe

Observed output immediately before the failure
----------------------------------------------
  created room: AF38V74B
  join ack ok; owner room-state update: ok
  livekit token: ok
  livekit room connect: ok
  owner signaling: ok (attempt 1)
  viewer signaling: ok (attempt 1)
  native camera frame roundtrip: ok (160x88, 56320 bytes)
  Falhou o fluxo real: token do backend -> fonte sintética Agora -> pixels no receptor nativo.
  Error: Process completed with exit code 1.

Diagnosis at stop point
-----------------------
LuniraAgoraRoundtrip.exe produced none of its own startup/signaling diagnostic
lines and the step ended in about five seconds. This means the failure happened
before the test reached its main test path. The leading hypothesis is a Windows
loader/runtime dependency problem in the Agora test executable. It is not an
Agora channel/token timeout: those paths have explicit diagnostics and longer
timeouts that did not run.

The pinned official Agora SDK archive was verified locally:
  Version: 4.6.2 FULL
  SHA256: 44D0CAABC2B5232B0416DF63845D88E45DE45681B9D32D99617DBD41BA8E6523

